    "dataset_kind": "market",
    "description": "Loss quantile (VaR) and expected shortfall of the portfolio over `horizon_days`, as a fraction of gross exposure, estimated from the most recent `window_days` of history. Portfolio weights are signed market value / gross exposure. Covariance methods (normal, student_t, montecarlo) use the asset covariance; historical, fhs and evt work on the historical portfolio return series. Multi-day: sqrt(h) scaling of the 1-day figure except montecarlo, which simulates N(h*mu, h*Sigma). Optional block bootstrap gives a 95% interval for VaR. The backtest always rolls the same method with a 250-day window over the whole history at 1-day horizon and the same confidence (Kupiec POF, Christoffersen independence, Basel zone on the last 250 forecasts).",
